# NOTE (2026-09-04, issue #1): three red-team ledgers that the scrub above
# initially swept in are STRUCTURAL, not operational — they describe the STRUCTURE
# of the already-public probe battery and this repo's own public code, and the
# standing red-team audit that runs in CI on the PUBLIC repo depends on them:
#   * redteam-uncontrolled-probes.csv        — B9/B11/E4 control-pairing exemptions;
#       absent -> validate_registration -> HARNESS BROKEN (this issue)
#   * redteam-callpath-parity.csv            — F-2 call-site guard-parity rules;
#       absent -> F-2 runs vacuous (false clean)
#   * redteam-canonical-resolution-exemptions.csv — F-3 canonical-resolver exemptions;
#       absent -> F-3 emits false-positive findings
# They are TRACKED (not ignored). Cleared by @security 2026-09-04 (no credentials,
# PII, or private paths); recorded in references/security-decisions.log.csv. The
# genuine weakness map (findings.log + accepted-weaknesses above, and
# security-decisions.log) stays private. Do NOT re-add these three to this list.
references/openweights-security-model-ratings.csv
